/**
 * Scene for "Named boxes and boxes that do not change" (lesson
 * c/variables-y-constantes, order: 4), a short film played on one persistent motion
 * canvas. The captions and cues live in `src/data/animations/variables-constantes-c.ts`.
 *
 * The canvas has two halves. The editor on the left is a fixed overlay that shows the
 * lesson's programs one at a time (the complete example, the uninitialized variable,
 * suffixed literals, the `const` assignment and the unparenthesized macro), each with a
 * bar that slides to the running line and the real output typed in the console below.
 * The viewport on the right holds the camera and an isometric world per program. A
 * variable is a box with a tag (its type and its name) and its value rests on top as a
 * pill; every instruction has a module on the rail that shows its editor line. The
 * light blue particle is the flow of execution; magenta marks the bug and the refusal
 * (the indeterminate "?", the assignment to a constant, the wrong result); violet marks
 * what handles it (the lock, the preprocessor, the fix).
 *
 * Palette: films are the approved exception to the Organic palette (DESIGN.md §8).
 * The colors are the `--xj-*` tokens declared once in the style block; nothing
 * else in the file uses a raw color.
 */
